+## Write pipeline (one invocation to a review package)
+
+`/generate-article` (or "write Medium article <topic/source/instructions>") runs the 21-step production pipeline through the deterministic CLI `scripts/write_pipeline` in the merged checkout `$HOME/Desktop/Projects/social-poster-fingerprint-eval` and stops at STOP for Max's review. The canonical instructions, sequence, schemas and budgets are in `generate-article.md` (`~/.codex/prompts/`); this section only tells Hermes when the pipeline applies. The CLI calls the existing `scripts.fingerprint_eval`, `scripts.medium_review` and `scripts.publish_route` modules and never publishes, schedules, or mutates Medium.
+
+Applies only when a run is started as `/generate-article` or when the caller's prompt names the pipeline. A caller that supplies its own contract keeps it. In particular the `youtube-playlist-to-medium-article` cron keeps following its prompt, `docs/hermes/weekly-youtube-medium-article.md` and the five `source-of-truth-*` skills unchanged; it does not call the pipeline CLI and does not depend on it being installed.
+
+```bash
+cd $HOME/Desktop/Projects/social-poster-fingerprint-eval && env HTTPS_PROXY= HTTP_PROXY= ~/.local/bin/uv run --python 3.12 --with markdown-it-py==4.2.0 python -m scripts.write_pipeline status --package <package-dir>
+```
+
+If `scripts/write_pipeline` is absent on the host, skip this section and use the generation workflow below.
+
+Pipeline notes for Hermes:
+
+- Order: sources, evidence and claim map, angle, author and fingerprint brief (`brief`, loaded before drafting), draft, fact check, editorial, voice, fingerprint repair, recheck, Medium review, title, images, independent critic, safe repair, fresh critic, final fingerprint verification (`fpverify`), integrity gate, hash, package, STOP.
+- Hierarchy: factual > source/link > semantic > quality > voice > fingerprint.
+- Semantic stages run on Sonnet through `claude -p` (subscription, API keys stripped). The CLI keeps state, hashes, cache, gates and metrics. Do not edit `write-pipeline/state.json` or the artifacts by hand.
+- The critic budget is 3 per run and never resets; upstream rework is limited to 1 per stage. If READY is unreachable, ship NOT_READY with the remaining findings.
+- The pipeline follows FRAMEWORK.md V6 and does not add a TLDR block, a Read next footer, or a bottom bio; the full-gate list below still governs the cron.
+- Fingerprint edits use our own metrics only. Never use or optimize against a third-party AI detector, and never conceal a required disclosure.
+- The final integrity gate runs `release authorize` with `FINGERPRINT_EVAL_WORKSPACE` pointed at the package's own `write-pipeline/workspace`, so it never replaces the production ACTIVE selector. Publishing still needs the normal `release authorize` and `release verify` in the production workspace for the exact bytes.
+- Real gaps become AUTHOR OPPORTUNITIES. Never invent experience, credentials, sources, quotes, numbers or results.
